    "id": "faraday_q003",
    "category": "specific_fact",
    "source": "Faraday Series I §17–26",
    "question": "Describe the bar-magnet helix experiment in §17: what were the magnet length and helix turn count, and what conclusion did Faraday state in §26?",
    "gold_answer": "A cylindrical bar magnet 12 inches long was thrust into a helix of 220 turns wound on a hollow pasteboard cylinder. While the magnet was at rest no deflection occurred; only on inserting or withdrawing it did a transient deflection appear. In §26 Faraday concluded that a conductor must cut across the magnetic curves of force to generate an EMF.",
    "expected_points": [
      "bar magnet 12 inches long",
      "helix of 220 turns",
      "no deflection while magnet at rest inside",
